  "notes": [
    "Each natural view is a fixed physics snapshot: first draw, one RAF wait, then eight sampled RAF/draw iterations.",
    "Controls contain only two sampled iterations each and are excluded from natural timing aggregates.",
    "Draw submission and first draw are elapsed CPU-side runtime.draw() calls, not GPU completion measurements.",
    "RAF wall intervals are performance.now() differences at successive RAF resumes and may include rendering, browser scheduling, and other work. They are not isolated GPU timings or hardware FPS.",
    "Prepare is wall time awaiting compileAsync and checking linked programs; setQuality and setCourse work is outside the prepare stopwatch.",
    "Generation times builtinWorldScene construction; load times runtime.loadScene. Values are copied across three quality records and deduplicated here.",
    "Round 1 is first-pass data in one run, not a controlled cold-cache/device baseline. All rounds use one runtime; qualities and views run in fixed order.",
    "WebGL renderer/vendor strings are generic; no device/GPU identification, VRAM, thermal or human acceptance conclusion. No timing threshold is asserted.",
    "Visibility is recorded at run start and at the end of each renderCase; it is not a continuous visibility/event trace. RAF outlier causes cannot be identified from this receipt.",
    "There are 21 natural RAF intervals above 1000 ms. This is a descriptive count, not an acceptance threshold. Tail outliers are retained in all aggregates."
  ],
